**Exploring PowerShell and Python**

In PowerShell, heredoc works differently. I can use `python -c` with triple quotes or employ `python` with stdin using `@' '@` to pipe input. However, just using `python - <<` doesn't do the job. The simplest method seems to be with `python -c "..."`, but quoting can be complicated. So, I'll create a temporary script using a PowerShell here-string piped into Python: `@' ... '@ | python -`. I think that will work!
