**Extracting specific sections**

It looks like the task involves inspecting sections 6, 8, and 9 separately to prevent truncation. I should script the outputs for each section individually and maybe redirect them to a temporary file for partial reading. Python will assist here, especially for section 6 in facts.md, focusing on field and validation messages. I want to extract only the first 200 lines of section 6, using Get-Content to pull the relevant information between markers. Let's print just that section with Python!
exec
"C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "Set-Location C:\\UI-specs\\URL-to-Code\\packs\\fxfer-v6\\screens\\file-transfer-tracking; @'
from pathlib import Path
import re
text=Path('facts.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
pat=re.compile(r'"'^## ('"\\d+)\\. .*"'$'"', re.M)
starts=[(int(m.group(1)), m.start()) for m in pat.finditer(text)]
starts.sort(key=lambda x:x[1])
r={}
for i,(n,s) in enumerate(starts):
    e=starts[i+1][1] if i+1<len(starts) else len(text)
    r[n]=(s,e)
for n in [6,7,8,9,10,11,12,13,15]:
    s,e=r[n]
    sec=text[s:e].strip('\\n')
    print('\\n'+'='*10+f' {n} '+'='*10)
    # don't spam: cap per section
    lines=sec.splitlines()
    cap=240
    for line in lines[:cap]:
        print(line)
    if len(lines)>cap:
        print(f'... ({len(lines)-cap} more lines)')
