**Evaluating newline handling in Python**

I'm exploring how the `\n` literal is interpreted. It looks like when I pass it to Python with `-c`, it includes `\n`. In PowerShell, it might be handled differently, but Python treats `;\n` as a line continuation, which causes issues. When Python sees this, it gives an error because of the unexpected character after the backslash. So, I should avoid using `\n` and just stick to semicolons instead. Let's figure this out!
